  "id": "airbone-gap",
  "term": "air–bone gap",
  "definition": "Air–bone gap is a hearing-related measure that, along with bone-conduction threshold, can be used before tympanoplasty to help predict hearing by air conduction after surgery. In counselling, it can support more realistic discussion of likely hearing outcomes and expectations.",
